(Photosynthesis and Plant Biology) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Photosynthesis is the process by which plants, algae and some bacteria convert light) Tj T*
(energy into chemical energy stored in sugars. The overall reaction combines carbon) Tj T*
(dioxide and water, in the presence of light, to produce glucose and oxygen. In plants,) Tj T*
(photosynthesis takes place inside organelles called chloroplasts.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Light-dependent reactions. The light-dependent reactions occur in the thylakoid) Tj T*
(membranes of the chloroplast. Chlorophyll absorbs mostly red and blue light and reflects) Tj T*
(green light, which is why leaves look green. The absorbed energy splits water molecules,) Tj T*
(releasing oxygen as a by-product. The reactions produce the energy carriers ATP and) Tj T*
(NADPH.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
