(The Calvin cycle) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Calvin cycle is the second stage of photosynthesis. It takes place in the stroma,) Tj T*
(the fluid-filled space around the thylakoids inside the chloroplast. The cycle does not) Tj T*
(need light directly, but it depends on the ATP and NADPH made by the light-dependent) Tj T*
(reactions.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Calvin cycle has three stages. In carbon fixation, the enzyme RuBisCO attaches) Tj T*
(carbon dioxide to a five-carbon sugar called RuBP. In reduction, ATP and NADPH are used) Tj T*
(to convert the resulting molecules into G3P, a three-carbon sugar. In regeneration, some) Tj T*
(of the G3P is used to rebuild RuBP so the cycle can continue, while the rest is used to) Tj T*
(make glucose and other carbohydrates.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
endstream
