(Factors that affect the rate of photosynthesis) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Several factors limit how fast photosynthesis can run. Light intensity matters because) Tj T*
(more light drives the light-dependent reactions faster, until the pigments are) Tj T*
(saturated. Carbon dioxide concentration matters because RuBisCO needs carbon dioxide for) Tj T*
(carbon fixation. Temperature matters because the enzymes involved work best at moderate) Tj T*
(temperatures; above about 40 degrees Celsius many enzymes begin to denature and the rate) Tj T*
(falls sharply. Water availability matters because plants close their stomata when water) Tj T*
(is scarce, which also reduces carbon dioxide intake.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The factor that is in shortest supply at a given moment is called the limiting factor.) Tj T*
(Increasing a factor that is not limiting will not raise the rate of photosynthesis.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
